1
00:00:02,713 --> 00:00:04,214
I'm Peppa Pig

2
00:00:04,816 --> 00:00:07,057
And this is my little brother, George

3
00:00:07,499 --> 00:00:09,340
This is Mummy Pig

4
00:00:09,781 --> 00:00:11,222
And this is Daddy Pig

5
00:00:13,545 --> 00:00:14,826
Peppa Pig

6
00:00:18,471 --> 00:00:20,284
"Tide Pools"

7
00:00:23,917 --> 00:00:27,517
Peppa and George are at the seaside
with Grandpa Pig and Granny Pig

8
00:00:33,068 --> 00:00:35,148
Peppa and George love the seaside

9
00:00:36,748 --> 00:00:38,580
Where's the sand?

10
00:00:40,432 --> 00:00:42,947
There's no sand on this beach, Peppa

11
00:00:42,987 --> 00:00:44,172
No sand?

12
00:00:45,067 --> 00:00:48,147
But we wanted to build sandcastles

13
00:00:48,387 --> 00:00:50,986
Peppa and George love building sandcastles

14
00:00:53,866 --> 00:00:55,153
Cheer up, George

15
00:00:55,194 --> 00:00:56,467
Don't cry

16
00:00:56,827 --> 00:00:57,945
On this rocky beach...

17
00:00:57,985 --> 00:01:00,121
There are still lots of exciting things to do

18
00:01:00,162 --> 00:01:01,789
Like what?

19
00:01:01,870 --> 00:01:03,790
When the sea goes out...

20
00:01:03,830 --> 00:01:07,472
It leaves little pools of water between the rocks

21
00:01:07,552 --> 00:01:09,758
They're called tide pools

22
00:01:10,291 --> 00:01:13,955
And in every tide pool made by the sea...

23
00:01:14,195 --> 00:01:16,316
There's something very special

24
00:01:17,677 --> 00:01:20,117
I can see something shiny

25
00:01:22,048 --> 00:01:23,730
It's a coin!

26
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:28,096
This coin could be pirate treasure

27
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:32,664
Let's collect everything we find

28
00:01:32,704 --> 00:01:33,633
Okay

29
00:01:33,673 --> 00:01:36,348
We'll put everything in George's bucket

30
00:01:38,792 --> 00:01:42,484
I wonder what surprise is waiting in this tide pool?

31
00:01:42,570 --> 00:01:45,695
There's nothing special in this tide pool, is there?

32
00:01:46,950 --> 00:01:49,700
There's always something in every tide pool, Peppa

33
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,061
Have a closer look

34
00:01:52,022 --> 00:01:53,664
There really is something!

35
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:54,865
Yes

36
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:55,786
There's a...

37
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:58,130
Ouch!

38
00:01:58,176 --> 00:02:00,512
A crab is pinching Grandpa Pig's finger!

39
00:02:04,071 --> 00:02:06,514
You're very naughty, Mr Crab!

40
00:02:07,871 --> 00:02:09,233
Look, George

41
00:02:09,273 --> 00:02:11,912
Mr Crab walks sideways

42
00:02:15,323 --> 00:02:17,485
George is pretending to walk like a crab

43
00:02:18,328 --> 00:02:19,890
Peppa wants to be a crab too

44
00:02:19,930 --> 00:02:21,752
We are naughty crabs

45
00:02:21,792 --> 00:02:23,815
Pinch...

46
00:02:25,906 --> 00:02:27,372
Pinch...

47
00:02:27,413 --> 00:02:28,411
Help!

48
00:02:28,452 --> 00:02:31,785
Two very naughty crabs are coming to pinch me!

49
00:02:31,826 --> 00:02:33,532
Pinch...

50
00:02:33,779 --> 00:02:35,779
We are very naughty crabs

51
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:37,626
Pinch...

52
00:02:39,104 --> 00:02:41,786
Shoo, shoo, you two naughty crabs!

53
00:02:41,847 --> 00:02:43,869
Back to your little tide pool

54
00:02:43,909 --> 00:02:44,970
That's true

55
00:02:45,190 --> 00:02:47,845
Let's go look at other tide pools

56
00:02:49,715 --> 00:02:51,316
What do you see?

57
00:02:52,452 --> 00:02:53,720
A shell

58
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:55,427
Can you hear the sound of the sea?

59
00:02:55,467 --> 00:02:57,150
What do you mean?

60
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:59,113
If you put the shell to your ear...

61
00:02:59,153 --> 00:03:01,075
You can hear the sea

62
00:03:04,475 --> 00:03:08,168
Wow, I can hear the sea!

63
00:03:11,657 --> 00:03:13,780
I love this shell!

64
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:14,900
George

65
00:03:14,981 --> 00:03:17,223
Can you find a shell?

66
00:03:18,985 --> 00:03:19,945
Shell

67
00:03:20,587 --> 00:03:22,508
That's not a shell

68
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:27,116
Peppa is right

69
00:03:27,156 --> 00:03:28,505
That's not a shell

70
00:03:28,545 --> 00:03:30,301
George has found a...

71
00:03:30,341 --> 00:03:31,445
Fossil!

72
00:03:31,485 --> 00:03:33,127
What's a fossil?

73
00:03:33,168 --> 00:03:37,576
A fossil is the bone of an animal from a long, long time ago

74
00:03:38,019 --> 00:03:40,739
From the time of the dinosaurs

75
00:03:41,099 --> 00:03:42,242
Dinosaur!

76
00:03:46,422 --> 00:03:48,823
Tide pools are so much fun!

77
00:03:48,863 --> 00:03:51,068
Yes, they're fun for us

78
00:03:51,504 --> 00:03:53,615
But not for this little fish

79
00:03:53,655 --> 00:03:55,906
A little fish? Where?

80
00:03:57,165 --> 00:04:00,303
Poor little fish, it's trapped in here

81
00:04:02,922 --> 00:04:07,523
The little fish says she wants to go back to the sea right now

82
00:04:07,683 --> 00:04:10,004
Maybe you can use George's bucket

83
00:04:10,044 --> 00:04:11,485
To rescue her

84
00:04:11,525 --> 00:04:12,809
Yes!

85
00:04:13,558 --> 00:04:15,999
Peppa rescues the little fish with the bucket

86
00:04:17,207 --> 00:04:19,127
Don't worry, Mrs Fish

87
00:04:19,167 --> 00:04:21,408
You'll be with your friends soon

88
00:04:25,169 --> 00:04:26,890
Bye-bye, Mrs Fish!

89
00:04:27,410 --> 00:04:28,330
Bye-bye!

90
00:04:37,959 --> 00:04:40,198
I love tide pools!
